# Postgres ARCHIVE access — migration and parity tooling ONLY.
#
# The trading application does not read Postgres. It has not since the
# 2026-08-19 cutover, and neither image carries a driver
# (tests/unit/test_app_has_no_pg_driver.py fails the build if one returns).
#
# The archive is still up, because `trading_bot` is a SHARED database:
# treesearch-service's 14 live tables are inside it and are re-created at every
# treesearch boot, and SmartGarden shares the same server. So the archive
# answers — with data frozen on 2026-08-19, no error, and no staleness marker.
# That is why this DSN lives here and NOT in `.env`: a DSN in the ambient
# environment is exactly how ~36 legacy scripts kept reporting July numbers as
# current.
#
# Load it EXPLICITLY, in the tool that needs it:
#     load_dotenv(".env.migration")
#     url = os.environ["PG_ARCHIVE_URL"]
#
# Tools that legitimately want it: scripts/check_converted_tables_have_data.py
# (dual-store parity), and in trading-service pg_quiescence / prove_mongo /
# migrate_all / purge_bad_data / build_migration_ledger / verify_translations /
# check_natural_keys / quality_census / pg_embeddings_to_mongo.
#
# Install the driver from requirements-migration.in; it is deliberately absent
# from requirements.txt.
PG_ARCHIVE_URL="postgresql://<DB_USER>:<DB_PASSWORD>@<YOUR_NAS_IP>:5433/trading_bot"
